-*- org -*-
* Unreleased
** New functionality
- Add ~pdf-form-minor-mode~ for filling in PDF forms
  + Click on a text field, checkbox, radio button, combo box or list to change its value, move from field to field with ~TAB~ and ~S-TAB~, or press ~C-c C-e~ to pick one of the visible fields by name. Save the buffer to write the values to the file.
  + The fields you can interact with are marked on the page, so you can see where they are: ~C-c C-s~ or the "Render Options" menu turns the marks off and on, and ~pdf-form-show-fields-color~ changes how they look.
  + Lists that allow several selections are read with ~completing-read-multiple~; editable combo boxes accept text that is not one of their items.
  + Click on a signature field, or use ~M-x pdf-form-signatures~, to see whether a signature is valid and who signed it. The certificate's revocation is not checked online. Requires poppler-glib >= 21.12.
  + Fields are shown by their tooltip, if the form gives one, rather than their internal name, and text fields refuse input longer than their limit.
  + Reset buttons work, and ~M-x pdf-form-reset~ resets the whole form (poppler-glib >= 0.90).
  + From Lisp, ~pdf-form-values~ returns a form's values by field name and ~pdf-form-fill~ fills one in, e.g. from an Org table; ~pdf-form-fill~ checks every value before changing anything.
  + Sign documents with ~M-x pdf-form-sign~, into an empty signature field (also by clicking on it) or a new one in a rectangle of the page, with a certificate from an NSS database (~pdf-info-nss-directory~, by default poppler's). Unsaved changes are saved first; the signed document replaces the file, and a copy of the unsigned one is kept in ~pdf-form-backup-directory~. Requires poppler-glib >= 23.07.
  + New epdfinfo commands ~getformfields~, ~setformfield~, ~setformfield-text~, ~resetform~, ~validatesignature~, ~setnssdir~, ~signingcertificates~ and ~sign~, and the ~form-fields~, ~form-reset~, ~signatures~ and ~signing~ features.
- Add ~pdf-pages-minor-mode~ for page operations on the visited file #60
  + Delete (~C-c C-o d~), extract to a new file (~C-c C-o x~), move (~C-c C-o m~) and rotate (~C-c C-o r~ / ~C-c C-o l~) pages, and insert (~C-c C-o i~) or append (~C-c C-o a~) pages of another PDF.
  + Works on the current page, /N/ pages with a numeric prefix argument, or a qpdf page range such as =3-5,8,10-z= with ~C-u~.
  + Uses the =qpdf= program (8.4 or later), see ~pdf-pages-qpdf-program~.
  + Refuses to touch a buffer with unsaved changes, replaces the file only after qpdf succeeded, and keeps previous versions for ~pdf-pages-undo~ (~C-c C-o u~).
- Flatten annotations and form fields with ~pdf-pages-flatten-annotations~ (~C-c C-o f~), so that filled-in forms and documents annotated with other editors look the same in every PDF viewer.  Filled-in form field values become part of the page; annotations without an appearance stream (which this package creates) stay interactive, hyperlinks are preserved, and a file attachment is replaced by the drawing of its icon.  Form field appearances can be regenerated while flattening, see ~pdf-pages-flatten-generate-appearances~; needs =qpdf= 11.8 or later.  The previous version is kept for ~pdf-pages-undo~.
- Sign documents with an image of your signature, ~M-x pdf-form-sign-with-image~
  + Choose an empty signature field or a rectangle of the page as for ~pdf-form-sign~; the image (a PNG file, ~pdf-form-signature-image~ by default) is placed there, keeping its aspect ratio, and flattened into the page right away, so the signed document looks the same everywhere.  The previous version is kept for ~pdf-pages-undo~.
  + This is a signature in the everyday sense, not a digital one: it does not certify who signed.  Needs poppler-glib >= 22.07 with PNG support in cairo and =qpdf= 11.8 or later.
- Add stamps showing a PNG image with ~M-x pdf-annot-add-image-stamp-annotation~: the image fills the selected region, keeping its aspect ratio, and becomes part of the PDF.  Moving the stamp keeps its image while the document is open; after saving and reopening, place it again instead of moving it.
- Add ~pdf-thumbs~ (~T~), a grid of page thumbnails
  + The grid reflows to the window width, labels each thumbnail with its page label, and highlights the current page. ~RET~ or a click shows a page.
  + Thumbnails render asynchronously, those in view first, so long documents open at once. They follow ~pdf-view-midnight-minor-mode~.
  + Mark pages with ~m~, ~u~, ~U~ as in Dired, then delete (~D~), extract (~X~), move (~M~) or rotate (~R~ / ~L~) them with the operations of ~pdf-pages-minor-mode~.
- Add ~pdf-a11y-report~ to review the accessibility of tagged PDFs
  + A conformance checker like veraPDF cannot judge reading order, the heading outline or whether alt text is real. ~M-x pdf-a11y-report~ lists what a person has to check: whether the document is tagged, its language and PDF/UA claim, untagged pages, fonts that are not embedded, every figure with its alt text (flagging missing, empty, generic and file-name alt text), the headings in reading order (flagging skipped levels) and the reading order of each page (flagging content read away from its page).
  + Every entry is a button that shows the element in the PDF and highlights it where its area is known.
- Add ~pdf-reflow~ to read a PDF's text reflowed in reading order (#359)
  + ~M-x pdf-reflow~ in a PDF shows its text in a buffer of its own, at the current page, so it can be read in a narrow window, at any font size, with a screen reader and with the usual commands for text.
  + For a tagged PDF the text comes from the structure tree: headings are shown as headings (scaled by level, folding with TAB in Emacs 29 or later, listed by ~imenu~), paragraphs are wrapped by ~visual-line-mode~, lists keep their labels, tables are shown as rows of cells and figures as ~[Figure: alt text]~.
  + For a PDF that is not tagged it shows the text of each page in the order poppler reads it, joined into paragraphs, and says that this order is a guess.
  + ~RET~ (or ~mouse-2~) on a block shows it in the PDF and highlights it; ~o~ does so without leaving the text, ~n~ and ~p~ move by block, ~M-n~ and ~M-p~ by heading, ~g~ reads the PDF again.
- Add ~pdf-layers~ to show and hide the layers (optional content groups) of a PDF
  + CAD drawings, maps and some decks or exams (answers on a hidden layer) put content on layers that a viewer may show or hide. ~M-x pdf-layers~ (~C-c C-l~ in ~pdf-layers-minor-mode~, enabled by default) lists them as a tree; ~RET~, ~SPC~ or ~t~ toggles the layer at point, ~+~ and ~-~ show and hide it. Showing a layer of a radio button group hides the others of its group.
  + Links that show, hide or toggle layers (set-OCG-state actions) now work like other links.
  + Which layers are shown is view state: it is not saved to the file, and reverting the buffer resets it.
- Edit a PDF's metadata with ~M-x pdf-misc-edit-metadata~
  + Lists the title, author, subject, keywords and creator in a buffer; edit them and press ~C-c C-c~ to apply or ~C-c C-k~ to cancel. ~e~ in the ~pdf-metadata-buffer-mode~ buffer (~I~) does the same, and the PDF Tools menu has an /Edit Metadata/ entry.
  + Applying marks the PDF buffer as modified: save it to write the metadata to the file, revert it to discard the change.
  + ~pdf-misc-set-metadata~ sets one field, ~pdf-misc-update-metadata~ several; both work from Lisp.
  + Only the document information dictionary is changed; poppler leaves the XMP metadata stream alone. When the title changes and the document's XMP has a different ~dc:title~ (which PDF/UA and accessibility checkers read), a warning of type ~(pdf-misc xmp)~ says so. ~pdf-misc-metadata-xmp-title~ returns the XMP title.
  + New epdfinfo command ~setmetadata~, with the Lisp wrapper ~pdf-info-setmetadata~. Writing metadata requires poppler-glib >= 0.46 and is reported as the ~writable-metadata~ feature.
- Create square, circle, line and stamp annotations #179
  + Select a region with the mouse, then ~C-c C-a r~ (square), ~C-c C-a c~ (circle), ~C-c C-a L~ (line) or ~C-c C-a S~ (stamp), or use the new "Add shape annotation" entry of the context menu.
  + A line goes from where a plain mouse drag starts to where it ends.
  + Squares and circles can be filled: set their ~interior-color~ property, or use "Change fill color" in the annotation's context menu.
  + Stamps use one of the standard icons in ~pdf-info-standard-stamp-icons~ (Approved, Confidential, Draft, ...).
  + These annotation types are now shown in the annotation list by default.
  + Requires poppler-glib >= 0.26 for square, circle and line and >= 22.07 for stamps; rebuild ~epdfinfo~ to get them.
- Create free text and ink (free-hand) annotations #82
  + ~C-c C-a f~ writes text on the page: it fills the selected region, or starts where you click, and is read in the minibuffer.  Editing the annotation's contents (e.g. by clicking on it) changes the text on the page.
  + Free text is black 12pt Helvetica on a transparent background by default; set ~font-name~, ~font-size~ and ~font-color~ in ~pdf-annot-default-annotation-properties~, or change them, and the background color, from the annotation's context menu.
  + ~C-c C-a i~ draws with the mouse: each drag is a stroke, and ~RET~ saves all strokes as one ink annotation.  Its ~line-width~ property sets the width of the strokes.
  + Both are also in the context menu, next to "Add shape annotation", and shown in the annotation list by default.
  + Requires poppler-glib >= 24.12 for free text and >= 25.06 for ink; rebuild ~epdfinfo~ to get them.
- New option ~pdf-annot-moveable-types~ to choose which annotations can be dragged around with the mouse; it now includes stamps and free text.
- Select words and lines with the mouse, as in other PDF viewers #30 #132
  + Double-click selects the word under the mouse, triple-click the line. Dragging after the double or triple click extends the selection by whole words or lines.
  + ~S-mouse-1~ moves the end of the selection to the click (~pdf-view-mouse-set-region-end~), keeping the word or line steps of a double or triple click.
  + The selection works with ~M-w~ and the markup annotation commands such as ~C-c C-a h~, and in ~pdf-view-roll-minor-mode~.
  + With ~pdf-sync-minor-mode~, double-click still jumps to the TeX source when the PDF has a SyncTeX file; ~C-mouse-1~ does so always.
- Add ~pdf-present~, a presenter view for giving talks from a PDF
  + ~M-x pdf-present~ opens an audience window with the current slide alone, covering another monitor (~pdf-present-audience-monitor~, or ~C-u M-x pdf-present~ to choose), and a presenter window with the current and next slides, the speaker notes, the slide counter (with page labels), the elapsed time and the clock.
  + Both are plain windows rather than fullscreen frames: switching a frame to fullscreen is slow, and Wayland compositors such as COSMIC ignore it.  Each window is made in its final size, so no slide renders twice while the display settles.  Window managers that honor positions put them on their monitors; on Wayland, where compositors place windows themselves — the auto-tiling one in Pop!_OS included — their rules for floating the =PDF Audience= and =PDF Presenter= windows say where they go.
  + While a slide is held, the coming slides are rendered into the cache during idle time — one slide every ~pdf-present-prefetch-delay~ seconds, up to ~pdf-present-prefetch-count~ of them — so moving on does not wait for rendering; a nil delay turns it off.
  + Speaker notes come from Beamer PDFs built with =show notes on second screen=right= (slide and notes side by side on each page) or =show notes= (separate notes pages, which the audience never sees); ~pdf-present-notes-layout~ detects which by default.
  + Set the talk's planned length (~pdf-present-talk-duration~, or ~d~ while presenting) and the presenter view counts down what is left of it, warning from ~pdf-present-talk-warning~ minutes on and showing overtime; the elapsed-time timer, the wall clock and the slide counter (with page labels) are always there.
  + ~T~ shows every slide as a thumbnail grid (the pdf-thumbs one) in the current-slide window; the audience keeps seeing the current slide, and picking a thumbnail, with ~RET~ or a click, jumps the presentation to it.
  + The deck's file is watched (~pdf-present-auto-reload~): when LaTeX rewrites it while presenting, it is read again and the slides re-detected once the file has settled, keeping the current slide and the timers.
  + Keys in both windows: ~n~ / ~p~ (also PageDown/PageUp and the arrow keys that clickers send), ~<~ / ~>~, ~g~ to go to a slide, ~b~ / ~w~ for a black or white screen, ~d~ for the talk length, ~t~ / ~r~ to pause or reset the timer, ~q~ to quit and restore the buffer, windows and frames.
- Export and import annotations as XFDF, the annotation exchange format of Adobe and other PDF editors
  + ~M-x pdf-xfdf-export~ writes the annotations of the visited PDF to an XFDF file (default: the PDF's name with ~.xfdf~); ~M-x pdf-xfdf-import~ reads them back into the visited PDF.
  + Use it to move annotations between copies of a document: grade one copy of an exam and send the XFDF file along with the blank original, rather than a modified PDF; other editors, e.g. Okular and Foxit, read the file too.
  + The type, page, rectangle, color, opacity, contents, author, subject, the marked-up text regions of markup annotations, the icon of text and stamp annotations, the interior color of squares and circles, and the popup rectangle and state survive a round trip.  Ink annotations are not exported (poppler cannot read their strokes back), and the vertices of a line are approximated by the corners of its rectangle.
  + New module ~pdf-xfdf.el~ with the options ~pdf-xfdf-export-types~ and ~pdf-xfdf-author~.

** Functionality improvements and fixes
- Annotation colors no longer get slightly darker each time a document is saved and reopened.
- The ~popup~ property of markup annotations, which ~pdf-info-editannot~ now serializes correctly, positions a popup at relative edges as everywhere else.
- Fix: A mouse click no longer activates an empty region #342
  + ~pdf-view-active-region-p~ was true after any click in the page, even without a selection. A click now only deselects, and ~C-mouse-1~ again adds to the active region instead of replacing it.
- Fix: Selecting text in a page with a slice (~s b~, ~s m~) signalled "Invalid image specification"

** API changes (for package developers)
- New server commands ~structure~, ~fonts~ and ~xmpmetadata~, with the wrappers ~pdf-info-structure~, ~pdf-info-fonts~ and ~pdf-info-xmp-metadata~.
  + ~structure~ needs poppler-glib >= 0.26; ~pdf-info-structure-tree-p~ tells whether the server has it (feature ~structure-tree~).
  + With its optional argument (~FULL~ in ~pdf-info-structure~), ~structure~ returns the whole text of each element for reading it, without the text of nested figures, and the numbering of list items.
- ~epdfinfo~ reports the feature ~image-stamps~; ~addannot~ accepts ~stamp~ with the extra argument ~image:FILENAME~ for a stamp showing the PNG image in FILENAME.  New function ~pdf-info-image-stamps-p~.
- ~epdfinfo~ reports the features ~shape-annotations~ and ~stamp-annotations~; ~addannot~ accepts the types ~square~, ~circle~, ~line~ (with optional start and end points) and ~stamp~ (with an optional icon), and ~editannot~ the properties ~interior-color~ and ~line~ and ~icon~ for stamps.
- New functions ~pdf-info-shape-annotations-p~, ~pdf-info-stamp-annotations-p~, ~pdf-info-free-text-annotations-p~ and ~pdf-info-ink-annotations-p~.
- New ~pdf-view-region-selection-style~ returns the selection style to read ~pdf-view-active-region~ with
  + A double or triple click makes a region that selects by ~word~ or ~line~ regardless of ~pdf-view-selection-style~. Code that passes the region's edges to ~pdf-info-gettext~ or ~pdf-info-getselection~ should use this function instead of ~pdf-view-selection-style~; ~pdf-view-active-region-text~ and the annotation commands already do.
- New server commands ~layers~, ~setlayer~ and ~ocgstate~, with the wrappers ~pdf-info-layers~, ~pdf-info-setlayer~ and ~pdf-info-ocgstate~; ~pdf-info-layers-p~ tells whether the server has them (feature ~layers~).
- ~pdf-info-pagelinks~ returns links of the new type ~ocg-state~.
- ~epdfinfo~ reports the features ~free-text-annotations~ and ~ink-annotations~; ~addannot~ accepts the types ~free-text~ and ~ink~ (with an optional line width and one or more strokes), ~editannot~ the properties ~font-name~, ~font-size~ and ~font-color~ for free text, and ~getannots~ reports the font of free text annotations.

* Version 1.3.0
** New functionality to improve overall user experience
- Add ~pdf-view-roll-minor-mode~ for continuous scrolling @dalanicolai @aikrahguzar #224
  + This highly requested feature enables smooth, continuous scrolling through PDF documents with multiple pages visible simultaneously. Enable with ~M-x pdf-view-roll-minor-mode~.
  + Smooth pixel-level scrolling across page boundaries
  + Multiple pages visible at once in tall windows
  + Works with ~pixel-scroll-precision-mode~ for trackpad scrolling
  + Configurable page margins via ~pdf-roll-vertical-margin~ and ~pdf-roll-margin-color~
  + Closes #18, #104
- Add ~pdf-annot-edit~ command for avy-style annotation editing @dalanicolai #224
  + Press ~e~ in ~pdf-annot-list-mode~ or use ~M-x pdf-annot-edit~ to quickly select and edit annotations using keyboard labels.

** Functionality improvements and fixes
- Isearch now searches across all visible pages in roll mode #224
  + When ~pdf-view-roll-minor-mode~ is active, isearch highlights matches on all displayed pages simultaneously.
- Link following works with multiple visible pages #224
  + ~pdf-links-action-perform~ (bound to ~F~) now shows labels for links on all visible pages.
- Annotations work correctly on the right page in roll mode #224
  + Text and markup annotations are added to the correct page when multiple pages are visible.
- SyncTeX jumps work with continuous scroll mode #224
  + Forward and backward sync correctly navigate in roll mode.

** API changes (for package developers)
- ~pdf-view-active-region~ now returns page information
  + The region format includes the page number for multi-page awareness.
- ~pdf-isearch-hl-matches~ signature changed
  + Now accepts a list of pages parameter for multi-page highlighting.

* Version 1.2.1
** Functionality fixes
- Fix: Replace obsolete ~registerv-make~ with ~cl-defstruct~ #333
  + The ~registerv-make~ function was removed in Emacs 30. This change updates pdf-tools to use the modern ~cl-defstruct~ approach for register support, ensuring compatibility with Emacs 30+.
- Fix: Use correct key function for filtering page links in pdf-virtual #327
  + Fixes an issue where virtual PDF page links were not filtered correctly.

** Native compilation fixes
- Fix: Resolve all native-comp warnings across multiple files #333
  + Added ~declare-function~ declarations to pdf-cache, pdf-info, pdf-util, and pdf-view to eliminate byte-compilation and native-comp warnings.
  + Fixed docstring formatting issues that caused native-comp warnings.

** Installation and platform compatibility improvements
- Add ~doas~ as privilege escalation fallback in autobuild #323
  + The autobuild script now supports ~doas~ (used on Alpine Linux and OpenBSD) as an alternative to ~sudo~ for installing dependencies.

** Infrastructure
- Move CI from CircleCI/AppVeyor to GitHub Actions
  + All testing now runs on GitHub Actions with a unified workflow for Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows.
  + Pre-built Windows binaries are now available as artifacts from CI runs.

* Version 1.2.0
** New functionality to improve overall user experience
- Allow creation of markup annotations without a text selection @astoff #191
  + This means that you can now highlight an exact region, for example on OCR PDFs! Just select the region by holding down the Meta key and dragging the mouse. Then invoke ~pdf-annot-add-highlight-markup-annotation~ (with ~C-c C-a h~) and voila!
  + Please note that *only the highlight markup annotation* is supported on rectangular regions.
- Add option to display page labels in mode line @rafaelbeirigo #331
  + PDFs with custom page labels (Roman numerals, section numbering) can now show these labels in the mode-line. Enable with ~pdf-view-mode-line-position-use-labels~.
- Add ~pdf-metadata-buffer-mode~ for the metadata buffer @aidan-hall #305
  + The metadata buffer now has its own major mode derived from ~special-mode~, allowing you to press ~q~ to close it.
- Add horizontal scrolling support via mouse wheel @aikrahguzar #234
  + ~mwheel-scroll-left-function~ and ~mwheel-scroll-right-function~ are now properly set in ~pdf-view-mode~.
- Allow ~scroll-other-window~ to work in pdf-view buffers @whatacold #280
  + You can now scroll a PDF buffer from another window using ~C-M-v~ and ~C-M-S-v~.
- Add gamma correction option to midnight mode @vizziv #329
  + New customization options for gamma correction to improve contrast of colorful text in midnight mode. Also fixes a color conversion bug (dividing by 256 instead of 255).

** Functionality improvements and fixes
- Allow setting ~selection-style~ via the Easy Menu @astoff #190
- Improve the experience of editing Annotations @astoff #192
- Enable ~pdf-view-dark-minor-mode~ automatically if the current Emacs theme is dark #166
- Fix: Use ~kill-current-buffer~ instead of deprecated ~kill-this-buffer~ @michaelmhoffman #330
  + Fixes keybinding issue in Emacs 30. Closes #287.
- Fix: Use absolute line number in ~pdf-sync-forward-correlate~ @haselwarter #222
  + Forward sync now works correctly in narrowed buffers.
- Fix: Support pdf-buffer bookmarks in workspace managers @aikrahguzar #188
  + Bookmark restoration no longer assumes the buffer is displayed, fixing errors with workspace managers like ~activities.el~, ~burly.el~, and ~tabspaces.el~.
- Fix: Suppress errors when scrolling past document boundaries with ~C-n~ / ~C-p~ @benthamite #303
  + ~pdf-view-next-line-or-next-page~ and ~pdf-view-previous-line-or-previous-page~ no longer throw errors at document boundaries when ~debug-on-error~ is enabled.
- Fix: Set slice to common bounding box across all pages @tpapp #326
  + ~pdf-view-set-slice-from-bounding-box~ now computes the bounding box from all pages, not just the current page. Closes #325.
- Fix: Annotation sync error "No such annotation" @bramadams #260
  + Refreshes annotations on the current page to keep buffer and file in sync. Closes #246.

